  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Why does a Deep Fishing code say invalid?",
      "a": "Deep Fishing codes are case-sensitive and they do not all use the same case. For example update4 is all lowercase but Update5 starts with a capital U, so copy each one exactly."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which Deep Fishing codes should I use first?",
      "a": "Start with the update codes like update8 and update7. They give Tide Bait plus a Luck Potion, which is the best combo for catching rare fish."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does the tidal1000 code still work in Deep Fishing?",
      "a": "It used to give a Tidal rod skin, but the most recent checks list it as expired. If it still works for you, that is a bonus."
    }
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Work on your cast timing. A clean, long throw sends your line into deeper water, and distance decides which fish you can reach.",
    "Put your first cash into Strength. Each upgrade adds throwing distance, which opens rarer water and fish that sell for more.",
    "Since one cast can hook several fish, a long cast into deeper water usually pays better than lots of quick throws near the shore.",
    "Sell your catch regularly. Cash only helps once it turns into upgrades, so do not let fish pile up while you could be throwing farther."
  ],
  "useRewards": "Meadow Bait comes from most codes, so use it for everyday fishing. Save Tide Bait and Luck Potions for when you can cast into your deepest water, since that is where the rarer fish are. Cash codes like ThanksforPlaying and Release are best spent straight on Strength. Redeem everything once the tutorial is done, then decide what to use now and what to keep.",
